WEBVTT

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.600
What did I tell you? What did I tell you?
What did I tell you? What did I tell you?

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.310
How could we have sunk this low?

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:38.520
Did you hear that unenthusiastic applause?

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.060
How can we be expected
to fulfill our mission

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:43.360
of making everyone happy
with your singing?

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.780
I-I'm sorry. It's my fault
for not doing a good job singing.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:52.280
There's nothing wrong with your singing!

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.450
Be more confident in yourself!

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:58.450
The only thing lacking is a stage
and audience worthy of your singing--

00:00:58.450 --> 00:00:59.620
nothing more!

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:00.750
If you had those things,

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:04.130
then fulfilling that mission
would be a mere walk in the park!

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:10.880
You're the only one, Antonio.
The only one who praises my singing.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.890
But of course I recognize your talent!

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.310
I'm your partner AI!

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:20.350
Someday, I'll provide you with
a stage environment worthy of you!

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:22.230
So--

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:25.520
Hey. Why are you laughing?

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.070
Because it makes me happy.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:29.780
I'm going to work really hard, okay?

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:34.320
So that someday,
I can become a singer worthy of you.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.910
I'll do my best, okay?

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:14.990
<i>AS YOU LIKE MY PLEASURE</i>

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:30.420
<i>I was born aiming for the light</i>

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:36.340
<i>Bound by a bond,</i>
<i>a thin string</i>

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:41.350
<i>From the fortune of</i>
<i>awakening for a mission</i>

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:48.150
<i>Spinning many proud memories</i>

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:53.030
<i>Into this world,</i>
<i>for your sake</i>

00:02:53.030 --> 00:03:00.450
<i>Gratitude and a bouquet filled</i>
<i>with the universe</i>

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:06.620
<i>Destiny, even fate,</i>
<i>please let them shine</i>

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:11.590
<i>The joy of being able to protect those</i>
<i>having fun and smiling</i>

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:14.970
<i>I admire,</i>
<i>I am admiring</i>

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:17.550
<i>I can become stronger</i>

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:22.850
<i>I want even my crying voice</i>
<i>to be heard like a song</i>

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:27.810
<i>To these dazzling times</i>

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:37.320
<i>I'd like you to entrust tears too</i>

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:43.240
"Ophelia's Suicide" left a
huge impact on later AI history.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.410
After all, it was the first ever
instance of an AI suicide,

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:50.380
EPISODE 8

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:50.380
ELEGY DEDICATED WITH LOVE -
MY ONE AND ONLY BELOVED PARTNER

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.410
basically considered taboo.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.210
activists had a field day.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:51.170
"She had a heart, she had a soul--

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:52.380
otherwise, she couldn't
have killed herself."

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.090
Therefore, she was the same as a human.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:56.260
Of course, the claim itself was absurd.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:58.970
But afterwards, a spate of similar
incidents erupted all over the world.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:00.470
The cause is yet unknown.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:03.220
However, this served to blur the lines
between humans and AIs,

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:06.350
and it became a huge catalyst
for AI assimilation into human society.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:10.400
That's the gist of "Ophelia's Suicide,"
a seismic incident in AI history.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.620
Do you find it hard to believe?

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:28.500
If so, then I won't stop you
from backing out.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.830
As we only need to stop her
before she does something rash,

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.250
this operation will be an easy one,

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:35.130
but that's not to say that our chances
of avoiding disaster are nil.

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:37.880
What a nag, going on and on
a mile a minute!

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:41.140
What kind of communication circuits
are you using as a reference?

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:42.510
You're going to end up forever alone.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:43.890
That's neither here nor there--

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:46.470
Now, the timing for this lighting...

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:49.560
In the first place,
for all your blathering about AI suicides,

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:51.980
Well, if possible, I'd like to delay it
and then light up the stage...

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:53.520
didn't I just take a header
right before your eyes?

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:53.520
Okay, got it.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.650
There's a big difference
between you and her.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:57.280
As much as it annoys me, you jumped

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.900
having calculated that I would
rescue you, didn't you now?

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:02.320
That doesn't count as suicide.

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.320
Thank you.

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:09.080
Right. I will sing with all my heart!

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:12.540
So that I... can become myself.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:17.880
Fine. Doubting you won't get me anywhere.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.090
And it does seem like there's
something on Ophelia's mind.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:24.430
All we have to do is
fix the problem, right?

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:27.060
H-Hold up, come back here!
What are you going to do?

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:29.060
What do you mean?
I'm going to talk to her.

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:32.350
If she is thinking of taking
her own life, I've got to stop her.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:35.770
It would be terrible to lose
a gorgeous voice like hers.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:36.730
Mainly because

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:39.490
the audience waiting so eagerly to
hear her sing would be devastated.

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:40.940
Listen to me!

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:41.900
There's no need to talk--

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.240
we just have to stop her
right before she kills herself.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.280
And the records show that she
commits suicide after her performance,

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.790
meaning today's audience will have
nothing to grieve about so please,

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:50.620
rest assured!

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:53.290
I'm not talking about
the immediate future here.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:55.170
We have to eliminate
the problem at its root.

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:57.590
Or else the same thing
could happen again, am I right?

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:58.170
But--

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:01.130
Are you sure you can carry out your
mission with stopgap measures like that?

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:03.550
I don't want to let her die.

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:05.470
Not today, not tomorrow,
or even the day after!

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:06.720
Diva!

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:11.890
Huh. As usual,
she refuses to listen to me.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:13.440
I don't know about her memory,

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:16.690
but at her core she's
basically the same, eh?

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:27.870
♬ With just one phrase ♬

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:34.160
♬ I was connected to courage ♬

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.160
Pathetic, isn't it?

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.210
Oh!

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:40.630
♬ Because for the first time
you gave me thanks ♬

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:40.630
Right after I made my debut,
I barely had an audience at all.

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:46.220
♬ And smiled at me ♬

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:45.220
I was still only tracing the octaves
with my voice back then.

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:48.470
So you went through a time
like that, too, Big Sister?

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:51.180
♬ Why is it ♬

00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:51.180
What's the matter?

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:57.310
♬ That I am always
taught things from you ♬

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:53.310
It's almost time for you to go on.

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:56.940
Oh, I have permission.
It's just that...

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:02.530
...I wanted to know how you all sing,
and for what purpose.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:02.900
♬ I can never surpass you ♬

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:06.200
You said the same thing
a little while ago.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:09.280
♬ I want to see you,
I want to know more ♬

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:08.490
Listen to me, Ophelia.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.330
Is there something distressing you?

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:15.830
♬ Even though I don't know the name
of this feeling yet ♬

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:11.580
What?

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:13.750
You know, like... yeah.

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:15.830
Like something that
makes you want to die?

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:16.740
So inept!

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:22.840
♬ I will start walking from here ♬

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:18.630
Shut up.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:20.880
Big Sister?

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:25.670
Well, remember what you said before?
"So that I can become myself?"

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:28.300
♬ Hurrying because I want to draw it ♬

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:28.300
Well...

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:33.720
♬ The shape of the future ♬

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:41.270
Antonio?

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:44.230
He was my support AI.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:47.860
Five years ago, he shut down.
Though it's not clear why.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:52.030
He's a sound AI who single-handedly
handled her stage lighting and audio.

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:55.580
His breakdown greatly affected
her subsequent performances,

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:58.580
should you believe the cheap
gossip of that time, that is.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:03.750
The tragic songstress,
singing on in the limelight,

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.090
undeterred by her partner's
unexplained breakdown.

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:09.640
And the tragic ending that saw her
commit suicide to follow him in death...

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:10.970
...is what led humans to hope

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:14.390
for the existence of
what they called love, or a soul.

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:16.640
I'm not distressed at all.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:19.440
Because I'm so lucky, you see.

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:22.560
Everyone at the small theaters
also cheered me on,

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:25.650
and Antonio always looked out for me
when I messed up.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:28.030
What kind of AI was he?

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:30.820
He was... somewhat cranky.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:33.620
And he was kind of a nag,
and a bit argumentative...

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:35.410
Really, just the tiniest bit, I mean.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:36.500
Hmm.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.410
What's that look in your eyes?

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:39.370
But...

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:42.540
He was my one and only beloved partner.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:44.750
Antonio was the only one, you see.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.630
Who kept saying that
he would let the whole world

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:50.510
know about my... about Ophelia's singing.

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:52.590
I have no distress at all.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:56.060
But I know that he'd tell me
that I could still do better.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:59.230
I've got to try to be
who Antonio wanted me to be.

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:01.310
I have to become her right away.

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:03.520
If that's not distress,
I don't know what is.

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:05.570
That's what's driven you
to sing until now,

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:08.400
and it's the reason you're about to
set foot on the Festival stage today.

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:12.030
You can't bring yourself to take credit?

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:17.120
It doesn't matter where I sing.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:20.210
The important thing is to sing my best.

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:24.380
A song that will allow me to fulfill
the mission that I was born for.

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:27.960
Is that what Antonio wanted?

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:31.130
Yes. And it's also what I want.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:33.050
Then take that look off your face.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:33.510
What?

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:37.890
Did Antonio teach you to take the stage
with that expression on your face?

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:39.180
No.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:52.070
We operate so that we can
carry out our missions, right?

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:55.780
Our mission to make people happy
with our singing.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:57.870
You have to keep carrying out
your mission.

00:09:57.870 --> 00:09:59.870
From now on--forever.

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.420
It's time, right?

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:05.580
Yes.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:09.760
Matsumoto?

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:10.960
What is it?

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:14.050
I just don't see Ophelia
killing herself after all.

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:15.930
Her singing, her mission,

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:18.850
her partner's death... that girl is
serious about facing up to all that.

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:20.600
There has to be some other reason.

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:23.440
I told you from the start that suicide
was an absurd notion.

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:26.770
Would you mind telling me now about
the man you had a brush with?

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:29.480
Can you promise me that
you won't run off once I tell you?

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:33.820
I certainly can. Because if I did that,
you'd only go rogue on me, wouldn't you?

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:36.700
It's him.

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:38.280
Mister Kakitani?

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:39.580
What's he doing here?

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:41.040
And looking like that?

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.250
There's no record of him existing
in the official history.

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:44.750
Matsumoto?

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:47.750
Who is he? Does he have
something to do with Ophelia?

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:48.960
I'm forced to admit that it would be

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.170
extremely challenging
to compute an answer...

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:52.920
...armed only with the information
that I currently have on hand.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:56.050
Would it kill you to just
say you don't know?

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:58.470
All right, then what was he to Vivy?

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:00.390
They did have some kind
of relationship, right?

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:03.520
He wasn't really someone who had
all that much to do with her.

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:07.440
Isn't that for me to decide?
It's me we're talking about, after all.

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:09.480
Shouldn't you head back now?

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:17.700
"He was my one and only
beloved partner"...

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:18.950
...did she say?

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:46.390
♬ Rain is dropping ♬

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:52.070
♬ From the high sky to the ground ♬

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:56.950
♬ The one and only kiss ♬

00:11:56.950 --> 00:12:02.990
♬ It is a crown of water ♬

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:03.990
Now that's a flawless performance,
wouldn't you say?

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:08.210
♬ Falling in love is ♬

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:07.210
That said, even in the official history,
everything was fine up to this point.

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:09.290
After this, she returns
to her dressing room,

00:12:08.210 --> 00:12:13.920
♬ A place where you can't predict ♬

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:12.670
where she goes over the next part
of her performance with the staff--

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:13.920
Are you listening?

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:18.880
♬ If you are caught in its arms ♬

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.210
Is there a problem?

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:18.130
No. What a lovely voice she has.

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:20.510
I just thought that with
an audience in front of her,

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:23.890
♬ You're happy even if you burst ♬

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:23.140
she'd blow that rehearsal
out of the water.

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:25.720
Would you mind
focusing on our project?

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:29.440
♬ Sacrificial love, DEDICATE ♬

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:28.690
Which requires neither sympathy
nor empathy for Ophelia,

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:30.690
but rather the resolve
to save the future!

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:34.150
♬ Raising a sorrowful voice ♬

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:34.570
Like I said, that can't be done unless
we do something about her distress.

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:37.950
♬ The dark eyes of the person ♬

00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:37.950
Oh, come on!
Pour your heart into it more, Ophelia!

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:40.660
♬ you want to dedicate to, ♬

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:39.110
Hmm?

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:45.040
♬ if you looked into them, ♬

00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:45.330
You're an AI
and you're going there, too?

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:51.670
♬ Let's head over to the other side of ♬

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:48.500
Huh! Vivy couldn't stop obsessing
out loud about that, either.

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.540
"What does it mean to
pour your heart into something?"

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:53.380
And "How can I pour my heart
into my singing?"

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:56.050
♬ Cold loneliness and sadness ♬

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:54.500
Vivy said that?

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:55.380
Yes.

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:57.340
Hmm...

00:12:56.050 --> 00:13:00.260
♬ Embrace me ♬

00:12:57.340 --> 00:13:00.260
So her distress was really basic, then.

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:01.470
Basic?

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:04.010
Yes. You don't get
more entry-level than that.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.060
Even you should be able to grasp--

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:09.480
Wait, you don't get it?

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:11.730
Even though you're an AI from the future?

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:13.480
I don't see how that's necessary.

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:16.070
I'm an AI created solely for
the sake of the Singularity Project.

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:18.740
It's pointless to analyze
a pastime such as singing.

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:22.030
You mean you didn't
agonize over it with Vivy?

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:25.080
Vivy and I didn't have
that kind of relationship.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:28.250
We only collaborated on
the Singularity Project, nothing more.

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:30.330
Then what kind of relationship was it?

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:31.670
Mm?

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:32.920
Where did that come from?

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:34.540
Don't dodge the question.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:36.420
I did it just now, too--

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:40.720
I'm working with you to learn about
my memories from when I was Vivy.

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:43.340
You know, the type who doesn't
feed a fish she's caught?

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:44.760
Mmm!

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:49.180
We have less than two hours
before I go on.

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:51.520
Hmm!

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:53.480
Oh, it was a real mess of a relationship.

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:57.320
Exactly the same kind of relationship
you and I have now.

00:13:57.320 --> 00:13:59.740
She was self-centered, and stubborn.

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:04.030
A little fool who would rush into action
without hearing me out.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:06.370
She was prone to manhandling me,

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:08.410
and did everything in berserk mode.

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:13.920
Let us carry out the Singularity Project.

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:15.210
Copy that.

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:16.710
Vivy.

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:20.130
And just when I thought that I could
look to her with some confidence...

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:21.670
She ended up...

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:39.190
It was because of that malfunction
that I left her out of this mission.

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:42.110
So I wasn't planning on
running into you, either.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:44.280
And yet there you were,
giving me an earful.

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:46.660
Then why did you rescue me?

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:48.280
Mm!

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:51.870
If I'd become expendable,
you could've just left me alone.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:54.670
And yet you protected me.

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:55.620
Why was that?

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:58.880
Because I was a necessary
factor for this project?

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.340
Well...

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:10.970
The show just ended, right?

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:13.100
There's that look again.

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:14.810
I'm going to see Ophelia.

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:16.730
There's no need for that.

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:22.440
I've already gained control
of every security camera on the premises.

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:24.400
Once Ophelia leaves her dressing room,
as per the official history...

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:27.530
Didn't I tell you that that would just be
a stopgap measure?

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:28.740
Diva! I'm talking to you!

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:31.330
It's Ophelia that I have to talk to.

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:32.870
Just back off and let me handle this.

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:34.540
Aren't we partners right now?

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:37.790
Although I wouldn't say that we're
on Ophelia and Antonio's level.

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:39.580
Oh, I know!

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:40.170
Huh?

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:42.500
If we save Ophelia, and save the future,

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.760
then I'll tell you the answer
to that question.

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:47.010
The extremely basic thing, okay?

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:49.800
Huh...

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:54.020
Mmm...

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:17.120
Matsumoto!

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:18.120
Wh-What is it?

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:19.710
Did something else already happen
in so short a time?

00:16:19.710 --> 00:16:21.750
That man is here!

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:22.540
Where are you?

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:24.000
S-14!

00:16:26.010 --> 00:16:29.180
There's nobody there.
What on earth are you talking about?

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:34.010
Diva! Come back here, will you?

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:35.180
Kindly refrain from going off-book--

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:37.810
That man might have something
to do with all this, right?

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:40.190
He might try to harm Ophelia
and make it look like suicide.

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:41.900
There's no record of that.

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:43.690
Ophelia hasn't made a move yet, either.

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:45.650
Please come back for now.

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:47.650
Diva!

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:53.240
You...

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:09.880
Diva!

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:14.430
Huh?

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:19.810
H-Hacking? Aside from my own?

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:24.770
Hold on, hold on, hold on!

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:27.940
How could I have missed this?

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:30.950
This Ophelia is... fake footage!

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:35.950
Diva! Diva! Diva!

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:37.790
Stay calm, stay calm,
stay calm, stay calm!

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:39.160
The crucial thing here is the mission!

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:41.420
Don't get your priorities mixed up!

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:26.290
What would a songstress
be doing here on such a lonely stage?

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:27.540
Who are you?

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:29.210
Nice to meet you, Ophelia.

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:31.260
My name is Matsumoto.

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:34.300
I apologize for not being able
to greet you in my completed form.

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:37.600
I know I might not be a pleasant sight,
but I'm pleased to make your acquaintance.

00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:41.020
Uh... um... who exactly are you?

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:42.310
Why are you here?

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:45.230
I am Diva's partner.

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:46.730
Big Sister Diva's?

00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:49.650
Yes. Although it's only temporary.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:52.360
I've come to stop you
from killing yourself...

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:55.160
...or to be precise,
from self-destructing.

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:58.740
To be honest, as a fellow AI,
it's hard to wrap my head around...

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:01.790
But I can imagine
the despair you're feeling.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:06.130
Ophelia. I would guess that
you're no longer able to stand it?

00:19:06.130 --> 00:19:07.750
The world has recognized your talent,

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:10.050
and you've performed at
a major venue like today's,

00:19:10.050 --> 00:19:13.470
but continuing to sing brings you
no satisfaction. And why not?

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:16.140
Because your mission to make everyone
happy with your singing...

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:19.930
...you've incorporated Antonio, an AI,
into that mission, haven't you?

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:21.810
But that opportunity
has been lost forever,

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:24.390
and it's inflicted a grave wound on you.

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:25.890
I've seen it before, you know.

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:29.190
A songstress AI who froze
when something similar occurred.

00:19:29.190 --> 00:19:31.900
And now you've triggered an error,
bringing you here--

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:38.320
Comical... how truly comical!

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.660
Ophelia, self-destruct?

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:43.830
Oh, yes, it's true--I have lost all hope!

00:19:43.830 --> 00:19:46.330
Because even if I get to sing
in a massive theater like this one,

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:49.420
no matter how much I try to glean
an answer from the other songstresses,

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:52.840
that still doesn't bring me any closer
to the ideal singing!

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:55.550
If you've come here to rescue me,

00:19:55.550 --> 00:19:58.390
then you're fatally late...
you're far too late!

00:19:58.390 --> 00:20:01.930
And why is that?
Because Ophelia is no more!

00:20:03.560 --> 00:20:06.100
I am Antonio!

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:43.280
My teacher loved that sound.

00:21:47.830 --> 00:21:50.370
Of all the lessons that I'd abandoned,

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:53.170
the one thing that
I stuck with was the piano.

00:21:53.170 --> 00:21:56.040
Like any kid,
I dreamed of becoming a pianist.

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:03.140
I was overwhelmed by my teacher's playing.

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:05.680
I admired what his fingertips could do,

00:22:05.680 --> 00:22:07.640
and catching up to him
was all that mattered to me.

00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:08.720
But...

00:22:17.570 --> 00:22:20.070
The ambulance will arrive soon.

00:22:20.070 --> 00:22:22.030
You must keep still, all right?

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:24.740
Tea--ugh!

00:22:28.240 --> 00:22:29.580
Wait...

00:22:30.580 --> 00:22:35.420
I want you to stay here. I mean,
you're a piano teacher, aren't you?

00:22:39.840 --> 00:22:45.140
My mission is to make everyone happy
with my piano playing, with my music.

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:49.350
Towards that end, I want you, Yugo,
and everyone else to stay alive.

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:30.510
It's been a long time, huh?

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:33.140
I've missed you.

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:34.270
Vivy.

00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:41.110
Why would you kill Ophelia twice?

00:23:39.360 --> 00:23:41.400
Come on, wake up! Vivy!

00:23:41.110 --> 00:23:43.240
My name is Diva. I'm not Vivy.

00:23:41.400 --> 00:23:43.240
And answer me!

00:23:43.240 --> 00:23:45.570
Damn you, defective AI!

00:23:44.240 --> 00:23:47.870
I am here so that I can
carry out my mission.

00:23:45.570 --> 00:23:47.870
Tell me, can you hear me?

00:23:47.870 --> 00:23:51.910
Can you hear the way I'm able to sing
such a wonderful song right now?

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:52.030
NEXT TIME

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:52.030
EPISODE 9

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:52.030
HARMONY OF ONE'S HEART -
MY MISSION, YOUR FUTURE
